camera: cam_icc_get_np() must not free the device a live icc path points at

What: put the throw-away device only when of_icc_get() failed; a returned path keeps it
(leaked at icc_put(), one small allocation per bus-client registration).
Hardening, not a 6.18 regression: same code ran on 6.12 (compat/cam_compat_612.h). Applies
after 0023.

Why / evidence:
- of_icc_get(dev, NULL) -> of_icc_get_by_index() -> path_init() stores the device:
  ack/drivers/interconnect/core.c:187 `path->reqs[i].dev = dev;` (6.12 core.c:185 same).
- cam_icc_get_np() then put_device(dev) -> cam_icc_dev_release() -> kfree(dev); the kobject
  name goes with it.
- Users of reqs[].dev afterwards: debugfs interconnect_summary (core.c:64-73,
  dev_name(r->dev) for every request on every node: the CPAS/ICP/IFE requests sit on the
  camnoc/mnoc nodes) and the icc_set_bw / icc_set_bw_end tracepoints
  (drivers/interconnect/trace.h:26, 62: __string(dev, dev_name(p->reqs[..].dev))), the latter
  fired by the icc_set_bw(path, 0, 0) right after the get (cam_soc_icc.c:111) and on every
  camera bandwidth vote. Reading the summary or enabling interconnect tracing (perfetto /
  atrace can) is a use-after-free.

--- a/drivers612/camera/work/compat/cam_compat_612.h
+++ b/drivers612/camera/work/compat/cam_compat_612.h
@@ -105,7 +105,15 @@
 	dev->of_node = np;
 	dev_set_name(dev, "cam-icc-%pOFn", np);
 	path = of_icc_get(dev, NULL);
-	put_device(dev);
+	/*
+	 * bsp618/port: a path keeps its device in path->reqs[].dev for its whole life
+	 * (dev_name() in debugfs interconnect_summary and in the icc_set_bw tracepoint), so the
+	 * throw-away device may only go with a failed lookup; a live path keeps it. It is
+	 * leaked at icc_put() (struct icc_path is core-private): one small allocation per
+	 * camera bus client registration.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(path))
+		put_device(dev);
 	return path;
 }
 
